Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Make Windows treat the RTC (hardware clock) as UTC, matching macOS and Linux.
; Without this, Windows stores local time in the RTC and every macOS/Linux boot
; shifts the clock by your timezone offset (the classic "clock drift" bug).
;
; Apply: double-click, accept the UAC prompt, then reboot.
; Revert: change the value to 00000000, or delete the RealTimeIsUniversal entry.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\TimeZoneInformation]
"RealTimeIsUniversal"=dword:00000001
